        "description": "As a user\nI want secure HTTP headers\nin order to have basic protection against XSS\n\n## As Is\n\nThere is basically no foundation yet for the application. Wisp does ship a selection of\nmiddleware to us, one of which is for strict CSP headers.\n\n## To Be\n\nA middleware function that sets a variety of important HTTP response headers that relate\nto security, such as `content-security-policy`, with actual values tuned according to\nbalance security and needs for the application.\n\nWithout CSP headers, any injected resource, such as JavaScript will be fetched/executed\nwithout scrutiny. Validation and sanitization is _still required_ to defend against\ncross-site scripting.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- CSP header present to limit trusted origins for script/style/image sources\n- Other headers are also used to increase security profile:\n  - <https://github.com/scott-ray-wilson/plume>\n  - <https://helmet.js.org/>\n\n## Quality Criteria\n\n- CSP header is tuned for maximum security:\n  <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CSP>\n- Headers are automatically included in HTTP responses from the backend server through\n  middleware.\n",
        "due_date": null,
        "id": "08acb4c0-c61c-4d48-95a3-8203004da763",
        "points": null,
        "position": 5,
